image": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_012_thumb.jpg", "page": "12", "label": "12", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/12"}, {"image": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_013_thumb.jpg", "page": "13", "label": "13", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/13"}, {"image": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_014_thumb.jpg", "page": "14", "label": "14", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/14"}, {"image": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_015_thumb.jpg", "page": "15", "label": "15", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/15"}, {"image": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_016_thumb.jpg", "page": "16", "label": "16", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/16"}, {"image": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_017_thumb.jpg", "page": "17", "label": "17", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/17"}, {"image": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_017-01_thumb.jpg", "page": "18", "label": "[18]", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/18"}], "tableOfContents": [], "summary": {"uri": "letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839", "series": "JSPPD", "urlTitleValue": "JSPPD6", "documentSeriesTitle": "Letter to the Church and Edward Partridge, 20 March 1839", "editorialPageNumber": "10", "isPageNumberPresent": true, "searchUrl": "/published/jsp/searchable/papers/21225849/21225849-0010.xml", "clearText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> according as his work shall be<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"13273992686452666433\"><a href=\"#13273992686452666433\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans54\"><span id=\"documenttrans54\">54</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Job 7:1.</p><hr></div></div></aside> and now beloved Brethren we say unto [you] that in asmuch as God hath said that he would have a tried people that he would purge them as gold<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"69458606287892466\"><a href=\"#69458606287892466\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans55\"><span id=\"documenttrans55\">55</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Zechariah 13:9; and Malachi 3:3.</p><hr></div></div></aside> now we think that this time he has chosen his own crusible wherein we have been tryed and we think if we get through with any degree of safty and shall have keept the faith that it will be a sign to this generation all together sufficient to leave them without excuse<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"17047891879621383552\"><a href=\"#17047891879621383552\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans56\"><span id=\"documenttrans56\">56</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Romans 1:20; and <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 16–17 December 1833 [D&amp;C\n101]\">Revelation, 16–17 Dec. 1833</a> [D&amp;C 101:93].</p><hr></div></div></aside> and we think also that it will be a tryal of our faith equal to that of Abraham and that the antionts [ancients] will not have were off whereof to boast over us in the day of judgment as being called to pass through heavier afflictions that we may hold an even waight in the balances with them but now after having suffered so grate a sacrifis and having pased through so grate a scene of sorrow we trust that a Ram may be caught in the thicket<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"10649044942744576448\"><a href=\"#10649044942744576448\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans57\"><span id=\"documenttrans57\">57</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Genesis 22:13.</p><hr></div></div></aside> speedily to releave the sons and daughters of Abraham from their <span class=\"josephswriting\">great</span><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"6559559611711949605\"><a href=\"#6559559611711949605\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans5\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of JS.</p><hr></div></div></aside><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span>anxiety and to light up the lamp of salvation<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"14430806107681840140\"><a href=\"#14430806107681840140\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans58\"><span id=\"documenttrans58\">58</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Isaiah 62:1.</p><hr></div></div></aside> upon their countinances that they may hold on now after having gone so far unto everlasting life. Now brethren conserning the places for the location of the saints we cannot counsyl you as we could if we were presant with you and as to the things that ware writen heartofore [heretofore] we did not concider them any thing verry binding<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"6027614283300976405\"><a href=\"#6027614283300976405\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans59\"><span id=\"documenttrans59\">59</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">This statement likely refers to church leaders’ ongoing deliberations regarding whether to purchase land and vacant buildings from <a href=\"/person/isaac-galland\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Isaac Galland</a> in <a href=\"/place/lee-county-iowa-territory\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Lee County</a>, Iowa Territory, and at <a href=\"/place/commerce-illinois\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Commerce</a>, Illinois, to provide shelter for the <a href=\"/topic/church-of-christ\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Latter-day Saints</a> emigrating from <a href=\"/place/missouri\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Missouri</a>. After JS learned about early negotiations in mid-February 1839, he wrote to church leaders in <a href=\"/place/quincy-illinois\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Quincy</a>, expressing support for the purchase. On 5 March, <a href=\"/topic/bishop\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Bishop</a> <a href=\"/person/edward-partridge\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Edward Partridge</a> explained in a letter to JS that church leaders were hesitant to make the purchase. (<a href=\"/paper-summary/letter-from-edward-partridge-5-march-1839\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/letter-from-edward-partridge-5-march-1839\" poptitle=\"Letter from Edward Partridge, 5 March 1839\">Letter from Edward Partridge, 5 Mar. 1839</a>.)</p><hr></div></div></aside> therfore we now say once for all that we think it most proper that the general affairs of the <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"11132568974148102573\"><a href=\"#11132568974148102573\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x4070\" topic=\"x4070\" title=\"Church of Christ\">church</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Church of Christ\"><p>The Book of Mormon related that when Christ set up his church in the Americas, “they which were baptized in the name of Jesus, were called the church of Christ.” The first name used to denote the church JS organized on 6 April 1830 was “the Church of Christ...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/church-of-christ\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside> which are nessisary [p. 10]</div></body></html>", "expandedText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> according <span class=\"deleted\">their</span> &lt;​as his​&gt; work shall be<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"7149886842438191711\"><a href=\"#7149886842438191711\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans54\"><span id=\"documenttrans54\">54</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Job 7:1.</p><hr></div></div></aside> and now beloved Brethren <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>we say unto [you?] that in asmuch as <span class=\"deleted\">good</span> &lt;​God​&gt; hath said that he <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>would have a tried people that he would purge them <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>as gold<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"13286195011986161427\"><a href=\"#13286195011986161427\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans55\"><span id=\"documenttrans55\">55</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Zechariah 13:9; and Malachi 3:3.</p><hr></div></div></aside> now we think that this time he has cho<span class=\"line-break hyphenate\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>sen his own crusible wherein we have been tryed <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>and we think if we get through with any degree of <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>safty and shall have keept the faith that it will be <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>a sign to this generation all together sufficient to leave <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>them without excuse<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"797932829298285107\"><a href=\"#797932829298285107\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans56\"><span id=\"documenttrans56\">56</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Romans 1:20; and <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 16–17 December 1833 [D&amp;C\n101]\">Revelation, 16–17 Dec. 1833</a> [D&amp;C 101:93].</p><hr></div></div></aside> and we think also that it <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>will be a tryal of our faith equal to that of <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>Abraham and that the antionts [ancients] will not have <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>were off [whereof] to bo[a]st over us in the day of judgment <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>as being called to pass through heavier afflictions <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>that we may hold an even waight in the balances <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>with them but now after having suffered so grate a <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>sacrifis and having pased through so grate a scene <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>of sorrow we trust that a Ram may be caught in the <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>thicket<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"6204989103712028472\"><a href=\"#6204989103712028472\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans57\"><span id=\"documenttrans57\">57</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Genesis 22:13.</p><hr></div></div></aside> speedily to releave the sons and daughters of Abr<span class=\"line-break hyphenate\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>aham from their <span class=\"deleted\">grate</span> &lt;​<span class=\"josephswriting\">great</span>​&gt;<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"13830403578793056315\"><a href=\"#13830403578793056315\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans5\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of JS.</p><hr></div></div></aside><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span>anxiety and to light up the <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>lamp of salvation<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"3397344629688602117\"><a href=\"#3397344629688602117\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans58\"><span id=\"documenttrans58\">58</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Isaiah 62:1.</p><hr></div></div></aside> upon their countinances that they <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>may hold <span class=\"deleted\">up</span> &lt;​on​&gt; now after having gone so far unto ever<span class=\"line-break hyphenate\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>lasting life. Now brethren conserning the places for <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>the location of the saints we cannot counsyl you as <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>we could if we were presant with you and &lt;​as​&gt; to the <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>things that ware writen heartofore [heretofore] we did not <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>concider them any thing verry binding<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"6329379571677297891\"><a href=\"#6329379571677297891\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans59\"><span id=\"documenttrans59\">59</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">This statement likely refers to church leaders’ ongoing deliberations regarding whether to purchase land and vacant buildings from <a href=\"/person/isaac-galland\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Isaac Galland</a> in <a href=\"/place/lee-county-iowa-territory\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Lee County</a>, Iowa Territory, and at <a href=\"/place/commerce-illinois\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Commerce</a>, Illinois, to provide shelter for the <a href=\"/topic/church-of-christ\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Latter-day Saints</a> emigrating from <a href=\"/place/missouri\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Missouri</a>. After JS learned about early negotiations in mid-February 1839, he wrote to church leaders in <a href=\"/place/quincy-illinois\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Quincy</a>, expressing support for the purchase. On 5 March, <a href=\"/topic/bishop\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Bishop</a> <a href=\"/person/edward-partridge\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Edward Partridge</a> explained in a letter to JS that church leaders were hesitant to make the purchase. (<a href=\"/paper-summary/letter-from-edward-partridge-5-march-1839\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/letter-from-edward-partridge-5-march-1839\" poptitle=\"Letter from Edward Partridge, 5 March 1839\">Letter from Edward Partridge, 5 Mar. 1839</a>.)</p><hr></div></div></aside> therfore we <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>now say once for all that we think it most proper <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>that the general affairs of the <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"4908305700580150070\"><a href=\"#4908305700580150070\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x4070\" topic=\"x4070\" title=\"Church of Christ\">church</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Church of Christ\"><p>The Book of Mormon related that when Christ set up his church in the Americas, “they which were baptized in the name of Jesus, were called the church of Christ.” The first name used to denote the church JS organized on 6 April 1830 was “the Church of Christ...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/church-of-christ\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside> which are nessisary [p. 10]</div></body></html>", "calendarsOfDocuments": [], "versions": [{"versionTitle": "Letter to the Church and Edward Partridge, 20 March 1839", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/1", "versionFeatured": "true"}, {"versionTitle": "Letter to the Church and Edward Partridge, 20 March 1839, as Published in <em xmlns:tei=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" xmlns:lds=\"https://ldsc.xmlref.com/local/ldschurch\">Times and Seasons</em>", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839-as-published-in-times-and-seasons/1", "versionFeatured": ""}, {"versionTitle": " History, 1838–1856, volume C-1 [2 November 1838–31 July 1842]", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/history-1838-1856-volume-c-1-2-november-1838-31-july-1842/81", "versionFeatured": ""}, {"versionTitle": "“History of Joseph Smith”", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/history-of-joseph-smith/333", "versionFeatured": ""}], "images": {"smallImageUrl": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_010_thumb.jpg", "mediumImageUrl": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_010_med.jpg", "largeImageUrl": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_010.jpg", "downloadImageUrl": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_010_download.jpg"}, "imageCredit": "", "facsimile": "", "dzUrlXml": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_010.xml", "classification": "Documents", "publishedStatus": "FinalContent", "accessionNumber": "430", "requestedPageNumber": "10", "numberOfPages": "18", "editorialTitle": "Letter to the Church and Edward Partridge, 20 March 1839", "cleanEditorialTitle": "Letter to the Church and Edward Partridge, 20 March 1839", "date": "March 20, 1839", "handwriting": "Handwriting of Alexander McRae and Caleb Baldwin, with insertions by JS", "footnotes": [{"id": "7149886842438191711", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Job 7:1.</p></body></html>", "number": 54, "type": "number", "toenote": "", "longcitation": null}, {"id": "13286195011986161427", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Zechariah 13:9; and Malachi 3:3.</p></body></html>", "number": 55, "type": "number", "toenote": "", "longcitation": null}, {"id": "797932829298285107", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Romans 1:20; and <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 16–17 December 1833 [D&amp;C\n101]\">Revelation, 16–17 Dec. 1833</a> [D&amp;C 101:93].</p></body></html>", "number": 56, "type": "number", "toenote": "", "longcitation": null}, {"id": "6204989103712028472", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Genesis 22:13.</p></body></html>", "number": 57, "type": "number", "toenote": "", "longcitation": null}, {"id": "13830403578793056315", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of JS.</p></body></html>", "number": null, "type": "scribal", "toenote": "", "longcitation": null}, {"id": "3397344629688602117", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Isaiah 62:1.</p></body></html>", "number": 58, "type": "number", "toenote": "", "longcitation": null}, {"id": "6329379571677297891", "text": "<html><head></head><body><p class=\"bottom_0\">This statement likely refers to church leaders’ ongoing deliberations regarding whether to purchase land and vacant buildings from <a href=\"/person/isaac-galland\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Isaac Galland</a> in <a href=\"/place/lee-county-iowa-territory\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Lee County</a>, Iowa Territory, and at <a href=\"/place/commerce-illinois\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Commerce</a>, Illinois, to provide shelter for the <a href=\"/topic/church-of-christ\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Latter-day Saints</a> emigrating from <a href=\"/place/missouri\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Missouri</a>. After JS learned about early negotiations in mid-February 1839, he wrote to church leaders in <a href=\"/place/quincy-illinois\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Quincy</a>, expressing support for the purchase. On 5 March, <a href=\"/topic/bishop\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Bishop</a> <a href=\"/person/edward-partridge\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Edward Partridge</a> explained in a letter to JS that church leaders were hesitant to make the purchase. (<a href=\"/paper-summary/letter-from-edward-partridge-5-march-1839\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/letter-from-edward-partridge-5-march-1839\" poptitle=\"Letter from Edward Partridge, 5 March 1839\">Letter from Edward Partridge, 5 Mar. 1839</a>.)</p></body></html>", "number": 59, "type": "number", "toenote": "", "longcitation": null}], "meta": {"/paper-summary-PageTitle": "Letter to the Church and Edward Partridge, 20 March 1839, Page 10", "/paper-summary-MetaTitle": "Letter to the Church and Edward Partridge, 20 March 1839, Page 10", "/paper-summary-MetaDescription": "according as his work shall be54See Job 7:1. and now beloved Brethren we say unto [you] that in asmu...", "/paper-summary-MetaUrl": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/10", "/paper-summary-MetaImage": "/bc-jsp/content/jsp/images/430/430_ms4583_1_71_010_thumb.jpg"}, "scribes": [{"id": "per1113", "name": "Alexander McRae"}, {"id": "per46", "name": "Joseph Smith Jr."}], "printVolumeLocation": "<a href=\"http://www.josephsmithpapers.org/articles/documents-volume-6-february-1838-august-1839\" class=\"externalLink\" xmlns:srchdoc=\"https://ldsc.xmlref.com/local/ldschurch/searchDocuments\" xmlns:lds=\"https://ldsc.xmlref.com/local/ldschurch\"><span class=\"title\">JSP,</span> D6:356–372</a>"}, "legal": {}, "disableVerticalScroll": true, "documentURI": "/published/jsp/searchable/papers/21225849/21225849-0010.xml", "searchOptions": [{"name": "| This Document", "value": "document"}, {"name": "| Full Site", "value": "site"}]}